#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:63
msgid "Installing Rhubarb for Linux"
msgstr "安装Linux版大黄"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:65
msgid ""
"To install Rhubarb, enter the following command in the shell depending "
"on your distribution."
msgstr "要安装大黄，请根据您的发行版在shell中输入以下命令。"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:67
msgid "Arch Linux: ``# pacman -S extra/rhubarb``"
msgstr "Arch Linux: ``# pacman -S extra/rhubarb``"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:69
msgid "Debian GNU/Linux: ``# apt install rhubarb``"
msgstr "Debian GNU/Linux: ``# apt install rhubarb``"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:71
msgid "Gentoo Linux: ``# emerge media-audio/rhubarb``"
msgstr "Gentoo Linux: ``# emerge media-audio/rhubarb``"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:73
msgid "Solus: ``# eopkg install rhubarb``"
msgstr "Solus: ``# eopkg install rhubarb``"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:75
msgid ""
"If you are using any other Linux distribution please refer to its "
"documentation or visit the `Rhubarb download page <https://github.com/"
"DanielSWolf/rhubarb-lip-sync/releases>`_ and download the latest "
"**Rhubarb-Lip-Sync-x.y.z-Linux.zip** file (where 'x.y.z' represent the "
"software version number)."
msgstr ""
"If you are using any other Linux distribution please refer to its "
"documentation or visit the `Rhubarb download page <https://github.com/"
"DanielSWolf/rhubarb-lip-sync/releases>`_ and download the latest "
"**Rhubarb-Lip-Sync-x.y.z-Linux.zip** file (where 'x.y.z' represent the "
"software version number)."

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:77
msgid "|rhubarb_extracted_linux|"
msgstr "|rhubarb_extracted_linux|"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:79
msgid ""
"Start OpenToonz and open the Preferences window with File  →  "
"**Preferences...**"
msgstr ""
"Start OpenToonz and open the Preferences window with File  →  "
"**Preferences...**"

#: ../../source/using_rhubarb_with_opentoonz.rst:81
msgid ""
"Insert the path **/usr/bin**, or a path pointing to where you've "
